# Everything not excluded here is sent to the Docker daemon on every build.
#
# The Dockerfile needs only six paths from the context — composer.json/lock,
# package.json/lock, vite.config.js, resources/ and docker/ — because the application
# code is bind-mounted at runtime rather than copied into the image. Without this the
# context was 2.4GB, and almost all of it was the provider feed stores under storage/.
#
# Anything the Dockerfile COPYs must stay OUT of this file; DockerContextTest fails if
# one of them is excluded, so a future COPY cannot be silently starved of its source.

# Runtime data. The per-provider and per-playlist SQLite stores live here and are the
# bulk of the context — gigabytes on a busy install.
storage

# Installed dependencies. The deps stage runs composer itself and the assets stage runs
# npm ci, so sending these is pure cost — and a stale host vendor/ must never be able to
# reach a build that is supposed to install its own.
vendor
node_modules

# Compiled assets. The assets stage rebuilds them from resources/.
public/build

# Secrets. None of these reach an image layer, but there is no reason to hand them to
# the daemon either.
.env
.env.*
certs
health/heartbeat.env
health/state

# History, CI config and local tooling.
.git
.github
.claude
CLAUDE.md

# Logs and rotated archives that accumulate in the tree.
*.log
*.log.*
